  "result": "JWT `exp` field = seconds since epoch. `Date.now()` = **milliseconds**. Off by 1000x.\n\n**Bug:**\n```js\nif (Date.now() > decoded.exp) // wrong \u2014 Date.now() always >> exp\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n```js\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > decoded.exp) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nOr convert `exp` to ms:\n```js\nif (Date.now() > decoded.exp * 1000) { ... }\n```\n\nBoth correct. First cleaner. Expired token check should also use `>=` not `>` to reject tokens expiring at exact current second.",
